WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
If your prep is the 48-hour MiraLAX prep, this video will walk you through

2
00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.340
exactly how to take it.

3
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.440
Just follow along step by step.

4
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.920
For this prep, you'll need three 238-gram bottles of MiraLAX powder and five

5
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:14.980
28-ounce bottles of Gatorade.

6
00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.520
Your Gatorade cannot be red or purple.

7
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.980
Stick to a different clear or light-colored flavor.

8
00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:25.580
This prep starts two days before your procedure, not one, so make sure you're

9
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:28.560
following the right calendar day for each step.

10
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:32.720
Starting two days before your procedure, you'll be on clear liquids only, no

11
00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.480
food, and you should drink as much as you can.

12
00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:40.600
Good options include clear chicken, beef, or vegetable broth, and bone broth.

13
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:44.760
Sports drinks like Gatorade, Powerade, or Propel, and juices like white cranberry,

14
00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:49.280
white grape, apple, limeade, or strained lemonade.

15
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:54.760
Black coffee or tea, iced tea, Kool-Aid, Sprite, seltzer, ginger ale, boost

16
00:00:54.760 --> 00:00:56.600
breeze, and water are also fine.

17
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.720
Along with popsicles, Italian ice, and jello.

18
00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:04.370
Just avoid anything red or purple, dairy products, orange juice, tomato juice,

19
00:01:04.370 --> 00:01:08.440
grapefruit juice, alcohol, or anything with a cream base.

20
00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:12.920
On top of that, drink an extra 8 ounces of a clear liquid every hour while

21
00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:14.000
you're awake.

22
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.520
At 5:00 PM, mix half a bottle of MiraLAX, about 3/4 cup, with one 28-

23
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:21.160
ounce bottle of Gatorade.

24
00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:25.560
Drink an 8-ounce cup of the solution every 15 minutes until it's gone.

25
00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:30.370
At 7:00 PM that same day, mix the remaining half of that MiraLAX bottle with a

26
00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:34.280
second 28-ounce bottle of Gatorade, and drink it the same way.

27
00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:36.680
An 8-ounce cup every 15 minutes.

28
00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:40.440
Continue drinking as many clear liquids as you can once that's done.

29
00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:44.730
The day before your procedure, you're still on a clear liquid diet, no solid

30
00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:45.320
foods.

31
00:01:45.320 --> 00:01:49.360
You'll repeat the exact same steps with your second bottle of MiraLAX.

32
00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:53.900
At 5:00 PM, mix half the bottle with a 28-ounce bottle of Gatorade and drink an

33
00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:56.480
8-ounce cup every 15 minutes.

34
00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:01.020
At 7:00 PM, mix the remaining half with another 28-ounce bottle of Gatorade and

35
00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.080
drink it the same way.

36
00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:07.540
The morning of your procedure, six hours before your arrival time, open your

37
00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:09.880
third and final bottle of MiraLAX.

38
00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:14.280
Mix half the bottle with your last 28-ounce bottle of Gatorade and drink the

39
00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.560
entire mixture over the next hour.

40
00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.240
You must drink all of the prep solution as directed, even if you're already

41
00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.520
passing clear liquid.

42
00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:25.440
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

43
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.840
the clearest view during your procedure.

44
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:33.000
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule and neither

45
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:34.160
of us wants that.

46
00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:38.000
Please drink plenty of liquids throughout the process to prevent dehydration.

47
00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:42.080
Staying hydrated will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

48
00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:46.260
However, do not eat or drink anything, including water, for four and a half

49
00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:48.240
hours before your arrival time.

50
00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:52.800
You may brush your teeth during this time, just don't swallow any water.

51
00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.970
If you use an inhaler, please use it as usual about 3 hours before your

52
00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:57.680
procedure,

53
00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:01.410
and bring all of your inhalers with you, you may be asked to use them again

54
00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.880
just before your exam.

55
00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:07.140
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom, applying

56
00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:11.200
a petroleum-based ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

57
00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:16.050
That's it. You've got this. Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay

58
00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:16.960
hydrated.

59
00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:20.990
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office. We're here

60
00:03:20.990 --> 00:03:21.680
to help.
